# Regression pin for #1423: YAML 1.1 requires a '.' in the plain-float form, so "1e-7" is the
# STRING '1e-7'. Sharpy's YamlScalarResolver used to defer to double.TryParse, which is far more
# permissive than YAML, and returned the float 1e-07.
#
# The LENGTH line is what makes this checkable by a stdout oracle at all: printed bare, the two
# arms showed `1e-07` vs `1e-7`, which the differential oracle's float-tolerant OutputComparer
# deliberately treats as equal formatting of the same number. A type divergence that prints as an
# equal number is invisible to a value comparison — the string's length is not. Keep the length
# line even though the values now agree; it is what would catch a regression back to float.
import yaml

def main():
    v = yaml.safe_load("1e-7")
    print(v)
    print(len(str(v)))
